      "side": 1,
      "message": "Lots of thoughts, some I think should be done now, some could be follow-ups. I think right now the mix of mutex+atomic is confusing and I think we should just use a mutex for now (really simple) as we sort through the rest of the lifetime/ref/return logics. But I outlined what I think is a way to get us to a single atomic and no mutex while still having different classes of ref for CB, usage, and cache.",
