      "side": 1,
      "message": "notifyARefIsZero asserts that the last removed ref is kUsageRef or kCache; ignoring the assert issue, it looks like this could end up having the resource returned to the cache twice, once for the usage ref hitting 0 and once for the command buffer ref hitting 0.\n\nIt should be that command buffer refs only preserve aliveness; they should have been returned to the cache earlier when the usage ref hit 0, since any future use would be enqueued after the current command buffer ref finishes. In the case of mapped resources, it\u0027s expected they take the extra work of holding on to a usage ref for the same duration as the command buffer ref so that it\u0027s not returned to the cache too early.",
